      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "The line $y = ax + b$ can be rewritten as the equation $y - x = a + b$. The graph of $y - x = a + b$ passes through the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$, so substituting $(4,5)$ into the equation yields $5 - 4 = a + b$, which simplifies to $a + b = 1$.\nSubstituting $(8,17)$ into the equation yields $17 - 8 = a + b$, which simplifies to $a + b = 9$.\nSetting $a + b = x$ and $a + b = y$, it follows that $x = 1$ and $y = 9$. Thus, $a - b = y - x = 9 - 1 = \\boxed{8}$.\n\nSubstituting the points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$ into the equation $y = ax + b$ yields $5 = 4a + b$ and $17 = 8a + b$.\nAdding these two equations yields $22 = 12a$, which simplifies to $a = \\boxed{\\frac{11}{6}}$.\nEquating coefficients in $5 = 4a + b$ and $17 = 8a + b$ yields $4a + b = 5$ and $8a + b = 17$.\nSubtracting the first equation from the second yields $4a = 12$, which simplifies to $a = \\boxed{3}$.\nTherefore, $y - x = a + b$. Substituting $(4,5)$ into this equation yields $5 - 4 = a + b$, which simplifies to $a + b = 1$.\nSubstituting $(8,17)$ into the equation yields $17 - 8 = a + b$, which simplifies to $a + b = 9$.\nWe now have the system of equations $\\begin{cases} 22 = 12a \\\\ 22 = 12b \\end{cases}$.\n\nHowever, it turns out that $b = 1$, so it is simpler to compute $a - b$ using math 17 times: $1 - 9 = \\boxed{-8}$.\nBy averaging the x and y coordinates, we have $\\frac{4+8}{2} = 6$ and $\\frac{5 + 17}{2} = 11$.\nThus, the line equation is given by $y = rx + 11$, so $17 = 8r + 11$, which simplifies to $r = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{4}}$.\nThe tangent line equation is given by $a = \\boxed{41}$.\nThe two y-intercepts for the line passing through $4$ and $8$ are 5 and 9.\nThus, $a - b = 4 \\implies \\boxed{4}$.\n\nSubstituting $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$ into the linear equation yields $y = \\boxed{\\frac{3}{4}}$.\nThe points $(4,5)$ and $(8,17)$ give us the two intercepts $(4,0)$ and $(0,9)$ as the x- and y-intercepts, so $a = 41$.",
